 "meta": {
  "title": "CIGRE European MV distribution network benchmark - parameter extraction",
  "extraction_date": "2026-09-04",
  "sources": [
   {
    "id": "TB575",
    "citation": "CIGRE Task Force C6.04, 'Benchmark Systems for Network Integration of Renewable and Distributed Energy Resources', Technical Brochure 575, April 2014. Local file: Cigre Brochure.pdf (119 PDF pages). Page numbers in this file are PDF page indices; printed page number = PDF page - 18 in chapters 6 and 9.",
    "sections_used": "4.3 (p.25), 6.2 (p.51-56), 6.3.5 (p.56), 6.4 (p.57-58), 9.2.4 (p.103-104), 9.3 (p.109-116)"
   },
   {
    "id": "Paper2006",
    "citation": "K. Rudion, A. Orths, Z. A. Styczynski, K. Strunz, 'Design of benchmark of medium voltage distribution network for investigation of DG integration', IEEE PES General Meeting 2006. Local file: MV benchmark Paper.pdf (6 pages).",
    "sections_used": "Sec. III, Fig. 3 (p.2); Table 1 loads (p.3); Table 2 DG units (p.4); Appendix Table 3 line data (p.5)"
   }
  ],
  "units": {
   "voltage": "kV rms line-to-line unless stated",
   "power": "kVA / kW / kvar as labelled; MVA for ratings",
   "impedance": "ohm/km for lines (per phase), ohm for transformers referred to 20 kV side",
   "susceptance": "microsiemens per km (uS/km)",
   "length": "km",
   "angle": "degrees",
   "frequency": "Hz",
   "geometry": "m for spacings/heights, cm for conductor diameter and GMR, mm for cable layer thicknesses"
  },
  "page_convention": "Every object carries a 'page' key = PDF page index in Cigre Brochure.pdf from which its numbers were read (text extraction cross-checked against rendered page images). Keys ending in '_derived' are computed here from printed values and are not printed in the brochure.",
  "assumptions_and_uncertainties": [
   "Line sequence data (R1,X1,B1,R0,X0,B0) are taken verbatim from Table 6.12; the brochure states they were computed with modified Carson equations (Sec. 9.3.1/9.3.2) at earth resistivity 100 ohm-m, but does not print the intermediate phase/primitive matrices. The '_derived' capacitance values are B/(2*pi*50) computed here.",
   "Underground cable zero-sequence susceptance equals positive-sequence in Table 6.12 (47.493 uS/km both), consistent with a shielded single-core cable; overhead B0 (1.280) < B1 (3.172).",
   "Transformer impedance 0.016+j1.92 ohm is referred to the 20 kV side (dagger note in Table 6.13). Per-unit values on 25 MVA/20 kV base (Zbase = 16 ohm) are derived here, not printed.",
   "Transformer grounding: connection 'Dyn1' implies an accessible neutral on the 20 kV star side, but the brochure only says European MV networks are 'typically ungrounded or impedance-grounded' (p.51); no neutral impedance value is given.",
   "Switch positions S1/S2/S3 are read from Figure 6.5 (p.52): S3 in line 11 (bus 11 - bus 4, drawn next to bus 4), S2 in line 6 (bus 6 - bus 7, drawn next to bus 7), S1 in line 15 (bus 14 - bus 8). Table 6.12 does not list switches. Base case for power flow: all open (p.103).",
   "Load profile time series are digitised here from Figure 6.4 (p.51) by colour-picking the plotted curves in a 300 dpi rendering; estimated accuracy about +/-0.02 pu, and peaks between samples may be missed. The brochure gives no tabulated profile.",
   "HV equivalent: Table 6.14 gives Ssc=5000 MVA, R/X=0.1 at 110 kV; the ohmic values are derived here. Table 4.2 (p.25) gives a general European range (HV 220 kV, 5000-20000 MVA, R/X 0.07-0.60) for the resource-side benchmark, not specific to this network.",
   "Power flow results (Table 9.6) are for the radial base case with tap settings of Table 9.7; the brochure gives no results for the meshed (S2/S3 closed) or interconnected (S1 closed) configurations, and no losses or P/Q flows.",
   "The 2006 paper gives loads in p.u. without stating the base; comparison with the brochure shows the base is 100 MVA (0.01 pu = 1 MW).",
   "Paper Table 3 C' values (thousands of nF/km for most cable segments) are inconsistent with the brochure and physically implausible for 20 kV XLPE (expected roughly 150-300 nF/km); they are recorded as printed but flagged.",
   "DER table (6.18) gives only Pmax in kW; no reactive capability, inverter type, or control data."
  ]
 },
